WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:07.530
To make a car, you need some seriously heavy
metal.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:13.310
Take iridium, a super tough atom with 77
protons.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:15.680
That's used to coat the tips.

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:16.640
Of spark plugs.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:25.620
Next on the heavyweight lineup comes gold
with 79 protons.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:32.230
This shiny conductor resists corrosion,
making it ideal for exposed electrical

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:33.010
connections.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:38.140
These connectors here for this airbag
assembly are gold.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:42.670
And so this thing can react really quickly
if there's an accident and save your life.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:50.350
The biggest atom in a car is lead with 82
protons.

00:00:54.530 --> 00:01:00.140
Only lead has the durability to deliver the
short burst of high power needed to start an

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:02.300
engine over and over again.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:15.150
But until very recently, how the universe
made these oversized atoms was a complete

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:15.840
mystery.

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:19.320
You can't make gold atoms in a normal star.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:24.270
You can't make gold atoms in a massive star
that's dying.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:30.720
In order to make atoms this big with this
many neutrons, you need a truly cataclysmic

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:31.410
event.

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:41.130
Just a few years ago, most scientists
believed that supernovas were cataclysmic

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:42.870
enough to do the job.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.660
But astronomer Edo Berger was not so sure.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:54.000
If you open any one of these books and flip
to the page that tells you where gold came

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.180
from, it will tell you that gold came from
supernova explosions.

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:04.190
But nobody had directly observed supernovas
producing elements like gold and inside

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.480
computer simulations.

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:09.980
Virtual supernovas lacked the energy to
forge these oversized atoms.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:13.010
Clearly, something was wrong.

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:18.350
But if supernovas weren't powerful enough,
what in the universe was.

00:02:18.710 --> 00:02:20.720
To form heavy elements requires a lot of
neutrons.

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:26.150
And so another possible theory was that the
heaviest elements were produced in the

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:28.280
mergers of two neutron stars in a binary
system.

00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:36.760
Neutron stars are some of the weirdest
objects in the universe.

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:41.710
They're formed from the collapsed cores of
big stars when they die.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:47.320
You're taking a couple of times the mass of
the sun and squeezing it down into a ball

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:49.240
that's only a few miles across.

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:53.170
The electrons and the protons that are
flitting around inside of that combine to

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:54.250
form neutrons.

00:02:54.250 --> 00:03:01.180
And what you're left with is an extremely
dense ball of neutrons about the size of a

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:01.810
city.

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:06.690
Neutron stars are extremely dense.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:12.720
If you take just a teaspoon of the neutron
star material, it's actually a billion tons.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:18.450
If neighboring stars die together, it's
possible for the two neutron stars they leave

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:22.460
behind to form a spinning binary pair.

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:25.170
But the partnership is doomed.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:30.480
What you're left over with is two incredibly
compact, dramatic objects spiraling around

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:40.120
each other. Over time, they move in together
until finally they can coalesce in the most

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:42.220
violent explosion since the Big Bang.

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:50.180
The explosion is called a neutron star
merger.

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:55.180
The amount of energy in this explosion is
crushing.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:57.750
There's almost no way to describe it.

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:01.900
It's like taking all of the sun's energy
that it will ever emit over its entire

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:04.390
lifetime and releasing it in a single
second.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:16.450
Berger suspects this colossal explosion
forges iridium gold and lead.

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:19.840
But to rewrite the textbooks, he needs hard
evidence.

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:26.110
It was difficult to convince the community
that this was a potential channel for the

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:27.610
production of heavy elements.

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:35.770
The proof is to actually see this process
happening in the universe.

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:45.600
June 2013, NASA's Swift satellite spots a
short burst of gamma rays from a nearby

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:52.430
galaxy. A sure sign that a neutron star
merger has just taken place.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:57.470
For Berger, it's the lucky break he's been
waiting for.

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:03.440
As soon as we knew that there was a gamma ray
burst nearby, we knew that this was our one

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:09.830
chance for perhaps several years to obtain
the right kind of measurements to test the

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:11.570
formation of heavy elements.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:19.000
Once Swift had identified the burst, the
Hubble Space Telescope swung into action to

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.110
capture images.

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:25.760
We grabbed them right away and we just
looked.

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:27.110
We knew exactly where to look.

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:28.880
At the center of this red circle.

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:32.150
And what we saw was this source right there
in the middle.

00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:37.790
That is the direct signature of the
production of very heavy elements, including

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:38.360
gold.

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:48.160
Berger's theory was right, but the rate of
production was way higher than he'd expected.

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:53.170
Well, in that one event, the amount of gold
that was produced was more than the mass of

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:59.730
the earth. If we can bring it all here, it
would be worth quadrillions and quadrillions

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:00.720
of dollars.

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:07.770
The theory is still very new, but it's
possible that ancient neutron star mergers

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:12.840
made all the heavy metals we see in the
world today, including the last remaining

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:14.550
ingredients for our car.

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:28.430
But all these elements are still floating
free in space.

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:36.680
What's needed now is to pull them all
together into one giant fabrication plant.

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:46.900
The earth. This is what your car looked like
before the earth was born.

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:50.710
Just a vast, swirling cloud of gas and star
dust.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:54.610
The exploded remains of ancient stars.

00:06:55.960 --> 00:07:00.550
The clouds between the stars of the galaxy
are made of everything that the earth, your

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:02.080
body and your car is made of.

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:06.850
There's everything that you need floating in
gaseous form between the stars.

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:10.470
4.5 billion years ago.

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:13.380
The gas and dust collapse once more.

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:19.160
It ignites explosively to create a new star.

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:22.790
Our Sun. Close to the young son.

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:25.030
All of the lighter stuff got blown away.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:27.650
What was left behind was the heavier, denser
stuff.

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:34.940
There was carbon, there was iron, there was
gold, everything in between.

00:07:38.510 --> 00:07:42.350
Over time, these free floating elements begin
to coalesce.

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:43.970
Dust becomes rock.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:48.170
Rocks joined to form larger objects called
Planetesimals.

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:52.930
Finally, Planetesimals joined to form the
Earth.

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:02.550
Our planet is born with all the ingredients
to build a car.

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:08.840
But those ingredients are about to go their
separate ways.

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:14.380
The Earth is a big planet and it's done
something that not all planets do.

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:15.550
It's differentiated.

00:08:15.550 --> 00:08:16.600
It melted.

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:24.690
Copper and lead dissolve in sulfur and float
to the top of the molten earth, making these

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:26.790
metals easy to mine today.

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:35.950
But precious metals like iridium and gold
sink to the core of the earth and most of the

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:37.180
iron sinks with it.

00:08:38.840 --> 00:08:39.980
It's kind of a pain, actually.

00:08:39.980 --> 00:08:43.550
All the heavy elements that are super
useful, like iron, they've sunk to the middle

00:08:43.550 --> 00:08:46.700
of the earth where we can't reach them and
there's not a whole lot of it in the crust.

